    <string name="tip_before_1_title">Prepare an emergency kit</string>
    <string name="tip_before_1_body">Water, non-perishable food, flashlight, radio, first-aid kit, documents and a whistle.</string>
    <string name="tip_before_2_title">Secure your home</string>
    <string name="tip_before_2_body">Anchor shelves and heavy objects; identify safe spots under sturdy furniture.</string>
    <string name="tip_before_3_title">Agree on a meeting point</string>
    <string name="tip_before_3_body">Choose a family meeting place and an out-of-town contact.</string>

    <string name="tip_during_1_title">Drop, cover and hold on</string>
    <string name="tip_during_1_body">Protect your head and neck under sturdy furniture until the shaking stops.</string>
    <string name="tip_during_2_title">Stay away from windows</string>
    <string name="tip_during_2_body">Avoid glass, façades and falling objects. Don’t use elevators.</string>
    <string name="tip_during_3_title">If you’re outdoors or driving</string>
    <string name="tip_during_3_body">Move to an open area away from cables and buildings; if driving, stop safely.</string>

    <string name="tip_after_1_title">Check for injuries and expect aftershocks</string>
    <string name="tip_after_1_body">Treat injuries, stay calm and be ready for aftershocks.</string>
    <string name="tip_after_2_title">Shut off the gas if you smell a leak</string>
    <string name="tip_after_2_body">Turn off the gas, don’t use flames or switches, and ventilate the area.</string>
    <string name="tip_after_3_title">Communicate by text message</string>
    <string name="tip_after_3_body">Use text messages to avoid overloading networks and check on your neighbors.</string>

    <string name="tip_mental_line_title">Mental-health line: %1$s</string>
    <string name="tip_mental_line_body">Free, confidential psychological support. If life is at risk, call %1$s.</string>
    <string name="tip_mental_1_title">Mental-health line: 192, option 4</string>
    <string name="tip_mental_1_body">Free, 24-hour national psychological support. In Bogotá you can also call Line 106. If life is at risk, call 123.</string>
    <string name="tip_mental_2_title">Your reactions are normal</string>
    <string name="tip_mental_2_body">Fear, insomnia, sadness or anger after a quake are common responses. Talk about how you feel and don’t face it alone.</string>
    <string name="tip_mental_3_title">Techniques to calm down</string>
    <string name="tip_mental_3_body">Breathe slowly (inhale 4s, exhale 6s), keep sleep and meal routines, and limit exposure to disaster news and images.</string>
    <string name="tip_mental_4_title">Support children</string>
    <string name="tip_mental_4_body">Listen to them, answer calmly and honestly, keep routines and remind them they are safe. Seek professional help if distress persists.</string>
    <string name="tip_mental_5_title">Support content (community)</string>
    <string name="tip_mental_5_body">Informational Instagram account: @saludmental_paracolombia. It’s a community resource, not an official emergency line; in a crisis use Line 192 (option 4) or 123.</string>

    <string name="tip_animals_1_title">If you evacuate, take your pet</string>
    <string name="tip_animals_1_body">Never leave it behind. Use a carrier or leash, bring water, some food and an ID tag with your phone number. Keep it close, tagged or microchipped.</string>
    <string name="tip_animals_2_title">Shelters receiving aid</string>
    <string name="tip_animals_2_body">Several affected foundations accept food, medicine and supplies (e.g. in Pereira, Armenia, Manizales and Villa María). Verify the channels before donating; many are shared via Protección Animal Javeriana.</string>
    <string name="tip_animals_3_title">Veterinary care</string>
    <string name="tip_animals_3_body">Vets and clinics are treating affected pets in quake areas (e.g. Royi Pets in Cali takes in disoriented animals). Confirm availability before traveling there.</string>
    <string name="tip_animals_4_title">Lost-pet finder</string>
    <string name="tip_animals_4_body">The community platform “Buscador de Personas y Mascotas — terremoto Colombia” lets you report and search for missing pets. It’s a community resource; verify details before acting.</string>
